{#-
	REYRE-WRT compatibility (v6, 2026-10-28): custom firmwares such as
	REYRE-WRT (Amlogic HG680P) patch the stock material footer with the
	two placeholder divs below. Their Status > Overview include
	(view/status/include/10_system.js) references the bare globals
	`tempcpu` and `cpuusage`, which the browser resolves via named
	access to these element ids, and their admin_status index polls
	admin/status/realtime/temp_cpu_combined to fill them. Without the
	divs the overview throws "ReferenceError: tempcpu is not defined".
	Ported 1:1 from the firmware's patched material footer.ut.
-#}
<div id="tempcpu"></div>
<div id="cpuusage"></div>
	<script>L.require('menu-boundless')</script>

</body>
</html>
